{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-941"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Activities of Business, Employers and Professional Membership Organizations - Administrative Coordination"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev4 "941"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :services/membership-association-coordination
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:operational-efficiency :administrative-transparency :member-services-access]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :membershipassocorg-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "MembershipAssocAdvisor ⊣ Governor (three HARD, permanent,
 un-overridable checks: member-unverified, effect-not-propose,
 scope-exclusion), a real compiled langgraph-clj StateGraph
 (langgraph.graph, membershipassocorg.operation/build: intake -> advise
 -> govern -> decide -> commit | request-approval -> commit | hold),
 rollout-phase gate (membershipassocorg.phase/gate, phases 0-3), and an
 append-only audit ledger + coordination log
 (membershipassocorg.store/append-ledger! + commit-record!, both a
 MemStore deftype and a DatomicStore backed by langchain.db via
 langchain-store.core). A back-office ADMINISTRATIVE COORDINATION actor
 for membership organizations (trade associations, chambers of
 commerce, professional bodies) -- not membership-eligibility,
 certification, advocacy-policy, dues-amount, or disciplinary-action
 authority. Five ops (`:schedule-member-event` /
 `:coordinate-dues-processing-logistics` / `:coordinate-supply-request`
 / `:schedule-staff-shift-proposal` / `:flag-safety-concern`), all
 `:effect :propose` only. `:flag-safety-concern` ALWAYS escalates to a
 human operator via the compiled graph's `:request-approval` node
 (`interrupt-before`, checkpoint-based resume); other ops auto-commit
 only once their phase enables them (phase 3 = full auto-commit).
 Every commit/hold/approval-rejected decision lands in the append-only
 ledger -- 34 tests / 75 assertions green (`clojure -M:dev:test`), demo
 runnable end-to-end against both Store backends (`clojure -M:dev:run`)."}
